post_remove() {
  cat <<'MSG'

omarchy-typewriter is removed, but the setup wizard could have created
things outside the package. If you used it, these may still be present:

  /etc/systemd/system/ollama.service.d/omarchy-typewriter-igpu.conf
      forces OLLAMA_IGPU_ENABLE=1 on ollama.service

  ~/.config/hypr/bindings.lua
      a "-- BEGIN omarchy-typewriter" block, now binding a missing command

  ~/.config/omarchy-typewriter/
      settings and, if you configured Cloudflare, an API token

  the local model, if you pulled one:  ollama rm granite4:micro-h

MSG
}

post_upgrade() {
  # Prompts under /usr/share are replaced on upgrade. Anything the user wrote
  # in ~/.config/omarchy-typewriter/prompts/ takes precedence and is untouched.
  :
}
